","correct":false},{"text":"ἄγει","correct":true}],"explanation":"Correct: ἄγει.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-3","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"nouns-cases-agreement","prompt":"What gender is ὁ ἵππος (“horse”)?","choices":[{"text":"masculine","correct":true},{"text":"feminine","correct":false},{"text":"neuter","correct":false}],"explanation":"Correct: masculine.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-4","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"nouns-cases-agreement","prompt":"The horse is the subject. Which case is used for ἵππος?","choices":[{"text":"accusative","correct":false},{"text":"genitive","correct":false},{"text":"dative","correct":false},{"text":"nominative","correct":true}],"explanation":"Correct: nominative.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-5","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"noun-adjective-agreement","prompt":"Choose “good” to agree with ὁ ἵππος (“the horse”; nominative singular).","choices":[{"text":"ἀγαθός","correct":true},{"text":"ἀγαθή","correct":false},{"text":"ἀγαθόν","correct":false},{"text":"ἀγαθήν","correct":false}],"explanation":"ἀγαθός agrees in gender, number, and case: masculine nominative singular.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-6","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"noun-adjective-agreement","prompt":"Choose “good” to agree with τὸν οἶκον (“the house”; accusative singular).","choices":[{"text":"ἀγαθός","correct":false},{"text":"ἀγαθή","correct":false},{"text":"ἀγαθήν","correct":false},{"text":"ἀγαθόν","correct":true}],"explanation":"ἀγαθόν agrees in gender, number, and case: masculine accusative singular.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-7","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"definite-article","prompt":"Supply the nominative singular article: ___ ἵππος (“the horse”).","choices":[{"text":"ὁ","correct":true},{"text":"ἡ","correct":false},{"text":"τὸ","correct":false},{"text":"τὸν","correct":false},{"text":"τὴν","correct":false}],"explanation":"Correct: ὁ.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-8","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"definite-article","prompt":"Which gender does the article show in ὁ ἵππος (nominative singular)?","choices":[{"text":"feminine","correct":false},{"text":"neuter","correct":false},{"text":"masculine","correct":true}],"explanation":"Correct: masculine.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-9","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"sentence-parts","prompt":"In “ὁ Ξενοφῶν τὸν ἵππον θεραπεύει.”, what is the function of “ὁ Ξενοφῶν”?","choices":[{"text":"subject","correct":true},{"text":"direct object","correct":false},{"text":"complement","correct":false},{"text":"transitive verb","correct":false},{"text":"intransitive verb","correct":false},{"text":"linking verb","correct":false}],"explanation":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν is the subject in this sentence.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"},{"id":"lesson-1-v2-grammar-10","type":"multiple_choice","topic":"sentence-parts","prompt":"In “ὁ Ξενοφῶν τὸν ἵππον θεραπεύει.”, what is the function of “τὸν ἵππον”?","choices":[{"text":"subject","correct":false},{"text":"complement","correct":false},{"text":"transitive verb","correct":false},{"text":"intransitive verb","correct":false},{"text":"linking verb","correct":false},{"text":"direct object","correct":true}],"explanation":"τὸν ἵππον is the direct object in this sentence.","sourceStatus":"Course-authored exercise"}],"modes":[{"type":"sentence-labeling","title":"Label Sentence Parts","instructions":"Label the function of each marked word or phrase.","labels":[{"code":"S","meaning":"subject"},{"code":"DO","meaning":"direct object"},{"code":"C","meaning":"complement"},{"code":"TV","meaning":"transitive verb"},{"code":"IV","meaning":"intransitive verb"},{"code":"LV","meaning":"linking verb"}],"items":[{"sentence":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν τὸν ἵππον θεραπεύει.","english":"Xenophon tends the horse.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν","answer":"S"},{"text":"τὸν ἵππον","answer":"DO"},{"text":"θεραπεύει","answer":"TV"}]},{"sentence":"ἡ μήτηρ τὸν ἄνδρα καλεῖ.","english":"The mother calls the husband.","tokens":[{"text":"ἡ μήτηρ","answer":"S"},{"text":"τὸν ἄνδρα","answer":"DO"},{"text":"καλεῖ","answer":"TV"}]},{"sentence":"ὁ Γρύλλος τὸν ἵππον ἔχει.","english":"Gryllus has the horse.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ Γρύλλος","answer":"S"},{"text":"τὸν ἵππον","answer":"DO"},{"text":"ἔχει","answer":"TV"}]},{"sentence":"ὁ κύων ὑλακτεῖ.","english":"The dog barks.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ κύων","answer":"S"},{"text":"ὑλακτεῖ","answer":"IV"}]},{"sentence":"ὁ Γρύλλος βαδίζει.","english":"Gryllus walks.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ Γρύλλος","answer":"S"},{"text":"βαδίζει","answer":"IV"}]},{"sentence":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν νέος ἐστιν.","english":"Xenophon is young.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν","answer":"S"},{"text":"νέος","answer":"C"},{"text":"ἐστιν","answer":"LV"}]},{"sentence":"ὁ οἶκος καλός ἐστιν.","english":"The house is beautiful.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ οἶκος","answer":"S"},{"text":"καλός","answer":"C"},{"text":"ἐστιν","answer":"LV"}]},{"sentence":"ὁ ἵππος ἰσχυρός ἐστιν.","english":"The horse is strong.","tokens":[{"text":"ὁ ἵππος","answer":"S"},{"text":"ἰσχυρός","answer":"C"},{"text":"ἐστιν","answer":"LV"}]}]},{"type":"matching","title":"Matching","instructions":"Match each Greek form or phrase with its meaning or grammatical function.","items":[{"prompt":"ἄγει","answer":"leads"},{"prompt":"βαδίζει","answer":"walks"},{"prompt":"βλέπει","answer":"sees or looks"},{"prompt":"θεραπεύει","answer":"tends or takes care of"},{"prompt":"ἔχει","answer":"has"},{"prompt":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν (ὁ Ξενοφῶν θεραπεύει τὸν ἵππον.)","answer":"subject"},{"prompt":"τὸν ἵππον (ὁ Ξενοφῶν θεραπεύει τὸν ἵππον.)","answer":"direct object"},{"prompt":"νέος (ὁ Ξενοφῶν νέος ἐστιν.)","answer":"complement"},{"prompt":"ἐστιν (ὁ Ξενοφῶν νέος ἐστιν.)","answer":"linking verb"},{"prompt":"ὑλακτεῖ (ὁ κύων ὑλακτεῖ.)","answer":"intransitive verb"}]},{"type":"fill-in-the-blank","title":"Fill in the Blank","instructions":"Type the missing Greek word. Press Return to check your answers.","items":[{"prompt":"___ μήτηρ μένει. (The mother stays.)","answer":"ἡ"},{"prompt":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν ___ τὸν ἵππον. (Xenophon tends the horse.)","answer":"θεραπεύει"},{"prompt":"ὁ κύων ___. (The dog barks.)","answer":"ὑλακτεῖ"},{"prompt":"ὁ πατὴρ φέρει ___ σῖτον. (The father carries the grain.)","answer":"τὸν"},{"prompt":"ὁ Γρύλλος βλέπει ___ θύραν. (Gryllus sees the door.)","answer":"τὴν"},{"prompt":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν νέος ___. (Xenophon is young.)","answer":"ἐστιν","accepted":["ἐστίν"]},{"prompt":"ὁ Γρύλλος ἔχει ___ ἵππον. (Gryllus has a beautiful horse.)","answer":"καλὸν","accepted":["καλόν"]},{"prompt":"ἡ ___ μήτηρ μένει. (The good mother stays.)","answer":"ἀγαθὴ","accepted":["ἀγαθή"]},{"prompt":"ὁ υἱὸς φέρει τὸ ___. (The son carries the water.)","answer":"ὕδωρ"},{"prompt":"ὁ νεανίας ___. (The young man rejoices.)","answer":"χαίρει"}]},{"type":"translation-builder","title":"Translation Builder","instructions":"Build each translation by choosing the subject, verb, and direct object. The spaces show the order to use in this exercise.","items":[{"prompt":"Translate into Ancient Greek: The mother carries the meal.","direction":"english-greek","choices":["ἡ μήτηρ","φέρει","τὸ δεῖπνον","τὴν μητέρα","μένει","ὁ ἵππος"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"ἡ μήτηρ"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"φέρει"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"τὸ δεῖπνον"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into English: ἡ μήτηρ φέρει τὸ δεῖπνον.","direction":"greek-english","choices":["The mother","carries","the meal","The horse","walks","the father"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"The mother"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"carries"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"the meal"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into Ancient Greek: Xenophon tends the horse.","direction":"english-greek","choices":["ὁ Ξενοφῶν","θεραπεύει","τὸν ἵππον","τὸν Ξενοφῶντα","ὁ ἵππος","λέγει"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"ὁ Ξενοφῶν"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"θεραπεύει"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"τὸν ἵππον"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into English: ὁ Ξενοφῶν θεραπεύει τὸν ἵππον.","direction":"greek-english","choices":["Xenophon","tends","the horse","The horse","walks","the father"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"Xenophon"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"tends"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"the horse"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into Ancient Greek: Gryllus has the water.","direction":"english-greek","choices":["ὁ Γρύλλος","ἔχει","τὸ ὕδωρ","τὸν Γρύλλον","ὁ σῖτος","βαδίζει"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"ὁ Γρύλλος"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"ἔχει"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"τὸ ὕδωρ"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into English: ὁ Γρύλλος ἔχει τὸ ὕδωρ.","direction":"greek-english","choices":["Gryllus","has","the water","The horse","walks","the father"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"Gryllus"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"has"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"the water"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into Ancient Greek: The son leads the horse.","direction":"english-greek","choices":["ὁ υἱὸς","ἄγει","τὸν ἵππον","τὸν υἱόν","ὁ ἵππος","φέρει"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"ὁ υἱὸς"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"ἄγει"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"τὸν ἵππον"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into English: ὁ υἱὸς ἄγει τὸν ἵππον.","direction":"greek-english","choices":["The son","leads","the horse","The horse","walks","the father"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"The son"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"leads"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"the horse"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into Ancient Greek: The father calls the dog.","direction":"english-greek","choices":["ὁ πατὴρ","καλεῖ","τὸν κύνα","τὸν πατέρα","ὁ κύων","ὑλακτεῖ"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"ὁ πατὴρ"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"καλεῖ"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"τὸν κύνα"}]},{"prompt":"Translate into English: ὁ πατὴρ καλεῖ τὸν κύνα.","direction":"greek-english","choices":["The father","calls","the dog","The horse","walks","the father"],"slots":[{"label":"Subject","answer":"The father"},{"label":"Verb","answer":"calls"},{"label":"Direct object","answer":"the dog"}]}]}]}}$bank$; l uuid; c jsonb; a jsonb; k text; block_row record;
BEGIN
 SELECT id INTO STRICT l FROM public.lessons WHERE slug='lesson-1';
 SELECT content INTO STRICT c FROM public.lesson_content_overrides WHERE lesson_id=l FOR UPDATE;
 a:=COALESCE(c->'activities','{}'::jsonb);
 FOREACH k IN ARRAY ARRAY['topic-practice','grammar-exercises'] LOOP
   a:=jsonb_set(a,ARRAY[k],(COALESCE(a->k,'{}'::jsonb)-'translationPerDirection') || (updates->k));
 END LOOP;
 UPDATE public.lesson_content_overrides SET content=jsonb_set(c,'{activities}',a),version=version+1,updated_at=now() WHERE lesson_id=l AND c->'activities' IS DISTINCT FROM a;
 FOR block_row IN SELECT b.id,b.content FROM public.lesson_content_blocks b JOIN public.lesson_segments s ON s.id=b.segment_id WHERE s.lesson_id=l AND b.content->>'source'='lesson_publish' AND b.content->>'kind'='activities' FOR UPDATE OF b LOOP
   a:=COALESCE(block_row.content->'value','{}'::jsonb);
   FOREACH k IN ARRAY ARRAY['topic-practice','grammar-exercises'] LOOP
     a:=jsonb_set(a,ARRAY[k],(COALESCE(a->k,'{}'::jsonb)-'translationPerDirection') || (updates->k));
   END LOOP;
   UPDATE public.lesson_content_blocks SET content=jsonb_set(content,'{value}',a),updated_at=now() WHERE id=block_row.id AND block_row.content->'value' IS DISTINCT FROM a;
 END LOOP;
END $exercises$;
COMMIT;
